From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Kuhn <martin@kuhn.host>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rpi5: fork DTs for firmware/U-Boot, mainline DTs for the
 kernel; HDMI console last

The boot partition shipped the kernel's mainline bcm2712 DTs at its root,
where the firmware picks the DT it hands to U-Boot. U-Boot does not come
up with the mainline DT (no HDMI, no network, reset after ~46 s); the
6.18 kernel in turn has no Ethernet with the downstream DT.

- partition root: the downstream DTs of the pinned firmware release
  (bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb, bcm2712d0-rpi-5-b.dtb, ...), matching overlays/
  (overlay_map.dtb, disable-bt-pi5/disable-wifi-pi5.dtbo). Byte-identical
  to what the v1.11.5.2 build shipped.
- dtb/broadcom/: the kernel's mainline DTs, which U-Boot's EFI boot loads
  as ${fdtfile} and hands to the kernel.

Kernel args: console=ttyAMA10,115200 (Pi 5 debug UART with the mainline
DT) then console=tty0 last, so /dev/console and thus the Talos logs are
on HDMI.
---
 artifacts/raspberrypi-firmware/pkg.yaml | 12 +++++++++++-
 installers/rpi5/src/main.go             |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/artifacts/raspberrypi-firmware/pkg.yaml b/artifacts/raspberrypi-firmware/pkg.yaml
index 3308cfe..7b8befc 100644
--- a/artifacts/raspberrypi-firmware/pkg.yaml
+++ b/artifacts/raspberrypi-firmware/pkg.yaml
@@ -18,7 +18,17 @@ steps:
         cp -v boot/LICENCE.broadcom /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/LICENCE.broadcom
         cp -v boot/COPYING.linux /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/COPYING.linux
         cp -rv boot/overlays /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/overlays
-        cp -rv /dtb/broadcom/bcm2712* /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/
+        # Firmware / U-Boot stage: the Raspberry Pi (downstream) DTs of this
+        # firmware release. The firmware loads bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb (C1) or
+        # bcm2712d0-rpi-5-b.dtb (D0) from the partition root, applies
+        # overlays/ and hands the result to U-Boot, which only works with
+        # these (it dies on the mainline DT).
+        cp -v boot/bcm2712*.dtb /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/
+        # Kernel stage: the mainline DTs of our kernel, where U-Boot's EFI
+        # boot looks for ${fdtfile} (/dtb/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb, or
+        # bcm2712-d-rpi-5-b.dtb on D0) and passes it to the kernel.
+        mkdir -p /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/dtb/broadcom
+        cp -v /dtb/broadcom/bcm2712* /rootfs/artifacts/arm64/firmware/boot/dtb/broadcom/
 finalize:
   - from: /rootfs
     to: /rootfs
diff --git a/installers/rpi5/src/main.go b/installers/rpi5/src/main.go
index 38cd824..29251d3 100644
--- a/installers/rpi5/src/main.go
+++ b/installers/rpi5/src/main.go
@@ -31,9 +31,12 @@ type rpiOptions struct {
 func (i *RpiInstaller) GetOptions(extra rpiOptions) (overlay.Options, error) {
 	return overlay.Options{
 		Name: "rpi5",
+		// The last console= becomes /dev/console, where Talos logs: keep
+		// tty0 (HDMI) last. The Pi 5 debug UART is ttyAMA10 with the
+		// mainline device tree.
 		KernelArgs: []string{
+			"console=ttyAMA10,115200",
 			"console=tty0",
-			"console=ttyAMA0,115200",
 			"sysctl.kernel.kexec_load_disabled=1",
 			"talos.dashboard.disabled=1",
 		},
